# HTML tags

## Line breaks

  First line
  second line
  third line
  fourth line
  fifth.

## Keys and marks

  Press `Ctrl`+`C` to copy, or `Page Down` to
  move on.

  Some text is marked as found, even in bold.

  A <kbd>key that never closes stays as
  source.

## Scripts: x² and H₂O

  Water is H₂O, x² + y² = rⁿ⁺¹ on the 2ⁿᵈ try,
  and xᵃⁱ keeps one size. Without script
  characters for every part, eiπ and a`b` stay
  plain.

## Details

  ▼ A summary with `Esc`

  The content is Markdown, as GitHub shows it:

  - one
  - two

  ▼ Written on one line

  The content & its tags are plain text.

  ▼ Details

  Without a summary, the block is called
  Details.

  - A list item

    ▼ Inside a list

    Content in the list.

  > ▼ Inside a quote
  >
  > Content in the quote.

  ▼ Outer, no blank line before the inner

  ▼ Inner

  Content of the inner one.

  Content of the outer one.

  ▼ With an HTML paragraph

  The paragraph's text, read as plain text.

  ▼ Text right after the end

  Content.

  Text after the details, in the same HTML
  block.

## Other tags

  Text with <b>bold</b> and <span>a
  span</span> stays as source.

  <div>
  A div block stays as source.
  </div>

  ▼ Never closed

  Runs to the end of the document.
